<title>USA: Typhoon continues to threaten shipping off Japan.</title>
<headline>Typhoon continues to threaten shipping off Japan.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Isa is weakening but continues to threaten shipping southeast of Japan, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Isa, with 105 mph winds, is in the western Pacific near 23.6n/139.8e and moving northeast about 14 mph. It will accelerate out to sea east of Japan, with top winds dropping to near 50 mph within 36 hours as the storm becomes extratropical.</p>
</text>
